---
/**
 * /budgeting-app
 *
 * Angle: Budget-focused users, expense trackers, YNAB-style envelope budgeters
 * Audience: People who want structured budgeting with expense tracking
 * Intent: "I want to budget my money and track my spending"
 *
 * Target Keywords (High Volume):
 * - budgeting app (100K-1M)
 * - budget app (100K-1M)
 * - budget planner (10K-100K)
 * - expense tracking (1K-10K)
 * - envelope budgeting (1K-10K)
 * - zero based budgeting (10K-100K)
 * - spending tracker (1K-10K)
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.budgetingApp;
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
>

  <AngleHero
    title="Finally, a budget that actually works"
    subtitle="Envelope budgeting meets daily expense tracking. Set categories, track spending, see exactly where every dollar goes."
    keyword="budget & expense tracker"
  />

  <div class="w-full overflow-x-clip -mt-52 md:-mt-[21.2rem] mb-0 relative z-10 flex justify-center">
    <div class="scale-[1.15] md:scale-100 origin-center w-max max-w-full md:w-[960px] md:max-w-none min-w-0 shrink-0">
      <img
        src={`/images/${meta.slug}/hero_light.png`}
        alt={meta.title}
        class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block dark:hidden"
      />
      <img
        src={`/images/${meta.slug}/hero_dark.png`}
        alt={meta.title}
        class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block hidden dark:block"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: The Envelope Method -->
  <Section
    heading="Zero-based budgeting. Every dollar has a job."
    bg="stone"
    class="mt-4 md:mt-0 !pt-12 md:!pt-2"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - What zero-based / envelope budgeting actually means
      - Give every dollar a purpose before the month begins
      - Digital envelopes replace physical cash envelopes
      - When an envelope is empty, spending stops (or you move money intentionally)

      Keywords to weave in: envelope budgeting, zero based budgeting, budget planner
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Explain the envelope budgeting philosophy. Every dollar gets assigned to a category before you spend it. When the category is empty, you're done — or you consciously move money from another envelope.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: How Finzen implements this digitally. Create categories, set amounts, watch the balances change as you spend.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Why this works when other budgeting methods fail — it's proactive, not reactive.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 2: Expense Tracking -->
  <Section
    heading="Track every expense. Build real awareness."
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Manual expense entry = intentional spending
      - Quick daily routine (2-3 minutes)
      - Real-time budget vs. actual
      - See spending by category instantly

      Keywords to weave in: expense tracking, spending tracker, track spending, money tracker
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: The power of manual expense tracking. When you enter each purchase, you become aware of your spending patterns.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Budget vs. actual in real time. Know instantly if you're on track or overspending in any category.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 3: Spending Categories -->
  <Section
    heading="Flexible categories that fit your life"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Customizable spending categories
      - Pre-built templates to get started
      - Subcategories for granular tracking
      - Category-level insights and breakdowns

      Keywords to weave in: expense categories, spending categories, category budgeting
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Custom Categories', detail: '[COPY: Create categories that match how you actually spend]' },
          { label: 'Starter Templates', detail: '[COPY: Pre-built category sets for common budgeting styles]' },
          { label: 'Subcategories', detail: '[COPY: Break down "Food" into Groceries, Dining Out, Coffee, etc.]' },
          { label: 'Category Budgets', detail: '[COPY: Set monthly limits for each category]' },
          { label: 'Rollover Options', detail: '[COPY: Unused budget rolls to next month or resets]' },
          { label: 'Category Insights', detail: '[COPY: See spending trends per category over time]' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 4: Cash Flow Visibility -->
  <Section
    heading="See your cash flow clearly"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Money in vs. money out
      - Spot spending leaks
      - "Where does my money go?" answered
      - Monthly and weekly views

      Keywords to weave in: cash flow analysis, cashflow, where does my money go
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Finally answer "where does my money go?" See income flowing in and expenses flowing out.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Spot the leaks — those small recurring expenses that add up. Subscriptions, daily coffees, convenience purchases.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 5: Visual Budget Reports -->
  <Section
    heading="Budget reports that actually help"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Visual progress bars for each budget category
      - Monthly spending summaries
      - Trend charts over time
      - Export options

      Keywords to weave in: budget visualization, spending reports, monthly financial report
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Budget Progress Bars', detail: '[COPY: See at a glance how much is left in each envelope]' },
          { label: 'Monthly Summaries', detail: '[COPY: End-of-month reports showing budget performance]' },
          { label: 'Spending Trends', detail: '[COPY: Track how your spending changes month to month]' },
          { label: 'Category Breakdowns', detail: '[COPY: Pie charts and bar graphs by spending category]' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 6: Beyond Just Budgeting -->
  <Section
    heading="Budget and invest in the same app"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Budgeting is step one — but what about investments?
      - Finzen combines budgeting with portfolio tracking
      - See the full picture: spending + saving + investing
      - Link to Investment Portfolio page

      Keywords to weave in: budgeting and investing
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Most budgeting apps stop at budgeting. But your financial life includes investments too. Finzen tracks both — so you see how your budget feeds your portfolio growth.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <CTABlock
    heading="Start your first budget today"
    subtext="Envelope budgeting + expense tracking. No bank connection required. Free to start."
  />

  <SiblingLinks slugs={meta.siblings} />

</Layout>
